---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Is it really free?',
    a: 'Yes. There is no trial, no ads, and no paid version.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need an account?',
    a: 'No. You can save, search, and restore tabs without an account. You need an account only for sync between your computers.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where are my tabs stored?',
    a: 'In your browser, in Chrome’s storage for extensions. If you turn on sync, a copy also goes to your account in Google’s Firebase service. Only your account can read it.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why does Chrome say that it can “read your browsing history”?',
    a: 'Chrome shows this warning for the tabs permission. The extension needs this permission to read the address and title of the tabs that you save. It reads them only when you save. It does not look at your history.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I move my tabs to a new computer?',
    a: 'Yes. Turn on sync and sign in on both computers. Or save a backup file (Settings, then Export JSON), and open it on the new computer (Settings, then Import JSON).',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which browsers does it support?',
    a: 'Chrome. Other browsers that are based on Chromium can install it from the Chrome Web Store, but we do not test them. There is no Firefox version yet.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens to my tabs if I uninstall it?',
    a: 'Chrome deletes the data of the extension. Before you uninstall, save a backup (Settings, then Export JSON), or keep sync on.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why is it called “I Hate Tabs”?',
    a: 'Because “I hate tabs” is what you said to your screen just before you looked for a tab manager.',
  },
];
---

<section class="px-6 py-24" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <p class="eyebrow text-center">FAQ</p>
    <h2
      id="faq-title"
      class="mt-3 text-center text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-5xl"
    >
      Questions that nobody asked
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-center text-text-secondary">We answer them anyway.</p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-3">
      {
        faqs.map(faq => (
          <details class="group rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 p-5 font-semibold transition select-none hover:text-accent-hover [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
              {faq.q}
              <svg
                class="size-5 flex-none text-text-secondary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <p class="px-5 pb-5 leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">{faq.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
